UX CASE STUDIES 
Case Study 1 — ActivMaths Teacher Dashboard 
• Challenge: Algerian math teachers needed to track 30+ students' progress without spreadsheets, with limited 
time and varying digital literacy. 
• Research: Informal interviews with teachers; identified they checked progress between classes (2-5 min 
windows). 
• Design: Glanceable dashboard with progress badges, color-coded urgency, single-tap drill-down. Mobile-first. 
• Outcome: Live in classrooms; teachers identify struggling students within seconds. 
→ dourous.activmath.dz 
Case Study 2 — BIOVATECH Hackathon Platform 
• Challenge: Convert visitors into team registrations across diverse audiences (biotech students, devs, designers). 
• Research: Benchmarked 8 hackathon sites; mapped user fears ("is this for me?", "do I need a team?"). 
• Design & Build: Bold hero with clear value proposition, modular sections per audience, single-CTA registration 
flow. Designed in Figma, built in HTML/CSS/JS, deployed on Vercel. 

• Outcome: 100+ participants registered for the event. 
→ biovatechhackathon.vercel.app 
Case Study 3 — Personal Portfolio — Biotech Meets Tech 
• Challenge: Communicate a hybrid identity (engineer + designer + developer) without confusing recruiters. 
• Design: Dual-narrative architecture; project cards designed for skimmability; visual system bridging scientific 
precision and design warmth. 
• Stack: Next.js, Tailwind CSS, fully responsive, deployed on Vercel. 
→ v0-portfoliobiotech31-gamma.vercel.app 
